DEAL DESCRIPTION

The thrust of the project is to capitalize upon the strategic location of the Caledonia peaker within the dual interconnect region between TVA and Southern Company (SOCO).  The purpose of this connection is to allow a direct connection from Caledonia to the SOCO system.  The project is beneficial for the following two reasons: (1) the SOCO over TVA premium (2) transmission constraints in TVA.  First, forward curves from the East Power Trading Desk indicate a premium to SOCO over TVA for at least the next three years, from 2001 through 2003.  Second, approximately 20 days per year occur where Caledonia can not sell power into TVA because of transmission constraints.  The strategic project enables Enron to better leverage the Caledonia peaker.

On August 24, 2000, Dave Delainey granted $900,000 in earnest money, to come out of Ben Jacoby’s budget, to facilitate the project.  The project completion is scheduled before the summer peaking season of 2001.The best case completion date is June 1; mid case completion date is July 1; and worst case completion date would be after July 1.

A new 500kv line will be erected from the Caledonia generation station to a new substation located within the Southern Company service territory.  The line length will approximately equal 3.2 miles, and line losses will approach zero given the short line length.  Double circuit poles instead of single circuit poles would add transmission flexibility but are contignent upon availability. 

Interconnect studies are underway to determine transient stability and load flow.  Completion of the studies is scheduled for 11/15/00.  Engineers project that the studies will conclude that no reliability conflicts exist with the progression of the project and will enable it to proceed.

An option agreement in which ABB Power T & D Company Inc. provides an option for (7) 500 KV circuit breakers and (14) air insulated switches to Enron North America Corp.  The option agreement with ABB was effective as of August 14, 2000.  Outside exercise date for the option remains the close of business September 15, 2000.

Discussions with CoGentrix and Calpine are underway to acquire right-of-way for the proposed new line.  The entire right-of-way looks like it may be bought for $2.5MM


















 




